  "report_week": "30",
  "report_period": "Week 30 (19th Jul to 26th Jul 2024)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Tokei Kaiun have committed their Capesize \"Cape Mathilde\" 178/2010 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) to Chinese interests at region USD 30 mill. Remind you that a couple of months ago, the two-years- younger \"El Grasso\" 181/2012 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at high USD 35 mill. Furthermore, following the sale of the \"Genco Maximus\" 169/2009 Sungdong, Korea (SS/DD 09/2024, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) & \"Genco Claudius\" 169/2010 Sungdong, Korea (SS/DD 01/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) back in March at USD 47 mill enbloc, clients of GENCO have now committed the sister vessel \"Genco Hadrian\" 169/2008 Sungdong, Korea (SS 12/2028, DD 11/2025, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Far Eastern interests at USD 25 mill. Castor Maritime announced the acquisition of the Ultramax \"Swansea\" 63/2015 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) from Norbulk Shipping at a price of USD 25,5 mill. Moreover, Taiwan Shipping committed their \"Tai Shine\" 61/2012 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS 10/2027, DD 08/2025, BWTS fitted) at region USD 22 mill. Remind you that the sister vessel \"Maritime Prosperity\" 61/2012 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS 11/2027, DD 11/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed back in April at same levels. On the Supramax sector, Nanjing Ocean Shipping committed their \"Heilan Cruiser\" 56/2012 Shanghai, China (SS 12/2026, DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) at excess USD 14 mill. Note that earlier this month, the \"Tristar Prosperity\" 56/2012 Cosco, China (SS/DD 06/2027, BWTS fitted) was sold at USD 15 mill. In addition, the \"Ionic Storm\" 56/2005 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 12/2025, BWTS fitted) of Ionic Holdings was committed to Greek interests at low USD 13 mill. Remind you that the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Ocean Glory\" 56/2006 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 09/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold back in April at low USD 13 mill also. The OHBS Handysize \"Coreleader OL\" 37/2012 Saiki, Japan (SS 10/2027, DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) of Oceanlance Maritime was committed to clients of Manta Shipping at USD 17,4 mill. For comparison, the \"Daydream Believer\" 37/2012 Onomichi, Japan (SS 03/2027, DD 01/2025, BWTS fitted, OHBS) was sold a couple of months ago at USD 17,6 mill.",
    "tankers": "Sinokor Maritime have committed their LR2 \"Pacific Jewels\" & \"Pacific Treasures\" 115/2016 Daehan, Korea (SS/DD 05/2026 & SS/DD 03/2026, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) to Vietnamese interests at high USD 60's mill each. Note that earlier this month, the two-years-younger Japanese built \"Pusaka Java\" 108/2018 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 01/2028, DD 03/2026, BWTS & Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 69 mill. The MR2 \"Nave Equator\" 50/2009 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 09/2024, BWTS fitted) of Navios Maritime was committed to Indonesian interests at USD 26 mill. Note that back in June, the sister vessel \"Gunmetal Jack\" 50/2009 Spp, Korea (SS 08/2029, DD 05/2027, BWTS fitted) was sold at excess USD 28 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia / China route continued throughout",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 13,000/15,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000/15,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 15,000/18,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via US East Coast into China were fixed around usd 25,000/27,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 22,000/23,000. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 17,250 pd for 4/6 months employment basis delivery China. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on a period at the usd 17,000 pd basis delivery South Korea for 2-year employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,000/19,000 pd. Indian Coastal trips were fixed around usd 9,000/10,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into India were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16.000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. West African trips via South Africa into China were reported at the level of usd 20,000/23,000 pd. US Gulf trips into China were fixed around usd 25,000/27,000 pd. South American trips into India were reported at the level of usd 17,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 700K. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A generally quiet week for this segment. South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 19,000/21,000 pd. On the period front, a Handysize was reported fixed in the usd 14,000 pd for 5/7 months employment basis delivery South East Asia."
    }
  },
